__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
.git/
.github/
reasoning/
logs/
releases/
*.env
# `**/` as well: an unanchored .dockerignore pattern matches from the context
# root only, and .devcontainer/local.env is a directory down. Nothing copies
# it into an image anyway -- this keeps it out of the context entirely.
**/*.env

# NOTE: config.json is deliberately NOT ignored. The runtime stage copies it to
# ~dev/.aws-batch/config.json, which is where endgame_aws's Config finds the
# bucket name. Without it every job dies at startup on FileNotFoundError.

# NOTE: models/ is deliberately NOT ignored either, despite being *.json. The
# batch manifest is derived from those configs at runtime, so they are what
# tells the array job how many children to run and which model each one is.
